 "clips": {
  "about": "Each kit thing that moves: its clips as its kind wrote them (what it is and how a player meets it, whether it plays at the start, whether it loops, its seconds). A clip of tracks is the glb's animation named in its `animation`, moving the bones of the kit mesh's skin. A clip of poses moves the parts it names: each pose a time and its morph target on the glb's kit mesh, null where the pose is the thing as it stands, each corner going in a straight line between two poses. Each joint is a bone a game may pose with no clip: `joint` its node among the skin's joints, `axis` in that node's own space, `range` the degrees from rest it may turn, and `couple` (where it has one) the joint whose turn drives it, `ratio` times over, as the thing's own linkage does.",
